      "answer": "The customer whose issue started after the 2026-02-20 taxonomy rollout is BlueHarbor Logistics. The proof plan proposed to get them comfortable with renewal is a 7-10 business day proof involving updating index weighting and adding a mapping layer to translate new taxonomy terms to old query terms for the top 20 saved searches. This includes running an A/B test to achieve a top-5 correct hit rate of at least 80%, compatibility testing with the EN-RULES-ENGINE to ensure no regression in suppression logic, and a conditional credit clause if the proof fails to meet the agreed metrics. The plan also involves a 90-day professional services engagement priced at $48k with a 30% discount if Orchestrator seat expansion is committed concurrently [art_0bccc580184e, art_bd3560dfe194, art_c9970c1dc932].",
