      "answer": "The SCIM fields conflicting at Aureum were \"department\" and \"businessUnit.\" Merchant Services used businessUnit=merchant while Payments Ops used department=payments, causing ingestion normalization to fail collapsing these into a single canonical attribute, which led to the Rules Engine failing to match entity tags for routing approvals. Jin proposed a fast fix by adding a preprocessing rule in Signal Ingest to map businessUnit to department (or vice versa) and publish a normalized field for the correlator. This fix is a config-only change, hot-reloadable, and does not require any Okta flow changes or appliance restarts, enabling a quick resolution without waiting for Okta change control. This approach was preferred over the longer-term standardization at the identity source, which would take 2\u20134 weeks due to change control processes [art_79f625aafa16].",
